SUMMARY:Sleepy Gap--Lake Powhatan  8 miles\, 1300'
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Place to meet**: Sleepy Gap Over
 look\, Blue Ridge Parkway Just past Mile Marker 397.\n**Description**: Hik
 e from the Blue Ridge Parkway\, along the Mountain-to-Sea trail\, through 
 Bent Creek and around Lake Powhatan\, then back to the BRP. Good footing\;
  mostly wide trails\; some nearby creeks\; nice view from Sleepy Gap. From
  Sleepy Gap east over Grassy Knob down to the MST down Stambaugh to Lake P
 owatan. Pine Tree to Explorer loop. Up to Chestnut Cove and back to Sleepy
  Gap. Type: Loop. Max elev: 3600’. Avg moving pace: 2.4 mph. Difficulty 
 (1=effortless\, 10=hard): 6.\nLunch at Stone Ridge following the hike is a
 n option!\n\n**\\*\\*Courtesy** (Please read carefully!)\\*\\* Only sign u
 p if you \\\\\\*truly\\\\\\* plan to come. If you must cancel\, please cha
 nge your status to "Not Going" as soon as possible. Avoid dropping out wit
 hin 24 hours so that wait-listers can have sufficient notice. And please p
 lease PLEASE don't be a no-show.\n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hiking Grou
 p event involves hiking and\, possibly\, transportation to and from the me
 etup site. Participants are responsible for their own safety and affirm th
 at they have the appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, equipment\, 
 and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and property. Neither yo
 ur hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can assure your safety nor el
 iminate all risks. By signing up for this event\, participant understands 
 and agrees.
