SUMMARY:Sam Branch Creek Scramble - 4 Waterfalls
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nThis is one of the steepest rock s
 crambles in the area. We will not be on a trail most of the time\, but in 
 the creek\, climbing up rocks. Most of the creek seems to be a continuous 
 waterfall. Both the Lower and the Upper Falls are spectacular to see. And 
 the views looking across the Shining Rock Wilderness are something to reme
 mber.\nIf you are confident when scrambling up and down rocks and walking 
 in the water you will be welcome to join us. This is the first time I have
  offered to lead this hike for the group. We will see 4 waterfalls\, inclu
 ding Sunburst Falls\, Lower Sam Branch\, Upper Sam Branch\, and Wash Hollo
 w Falls.\nWe will do this as an up and back. Elevation gain is approximate
 ly 1\,200 feet and the distance is approx. 3 miles.\nWe do not expect a la
 rge group of participants since not everyone would like this challenge.\nW
 e will meet at the Sam Branch Falls parking (35.338265\, -82.903358) on St
 ate Hwy 215.\n\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event may involve risks to one
 self and property. Participants\, by joining this hike\, affirm that they 
 have the appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, equipment and suppli
 es. Neither your hike organizer nor the Asheville Hiking Group can elimina
 te risks or be responsible for your well-being. Participants assume full r
 esponsibililty for any injuries\, damages\, or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315346294
 /
